# What the Vercel CLI uploads.
#
# The CLI takes the working directory, not a git tree.  If this file exists it
# REPLACES .gitignore as the upload filter -- so everything .gitignore was
# quietly keeping out has to be listed again here, or a deployment carries
# 380 MB it cannot use.  That precedence is the whole reason this file is not
# one line long (D15.4).

# 301 MB, built for darwin, useless to a Linux build.
.venv

# The dashboard is a separate Vercel project, deployed from ui/ (D15.6).
ui

# Tool and editor state.
__pycache__
*.pyc
.git
.claude
.vercel
.DS_Store

# `vercel link` writes .env.local, and it holds a VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN.  The CLI
# added it to .gitignore, which does nothing here -- this file replaced that
# filter (D15.4).  A credential does not belong in a function bundle, and
# api/test_deploy.py now fails if one is in the upload set (D15.12).
.env*

# The ARGO working set: 177 MB of pipeline inputs the API never opens.
# data/rag is deliberately NOT listed.  Its two files are the only thing under
# data/ the running API reads (api/retrieval.py:47), they weigh 706 KB, and
# without them /ask answers "no index built" (D15.5).
data/index
data/parsed
data/profiles
data/regions

# The README's screenshots.  1.5 MB of PNGs that only GitHub ever renders --
# no code path opens them, and a function bundle is not a place to keep
# documentation.
docs

# The pipeline itself.  Nothing under these paths runs on a serverless
# function, and nothing under api/ opens a file in them.
etl
db
run_pipeline.py
